# Private workspace guide

This directory is the ignored, local memory layer for one person. It is created by
`./cv init` and must never be committed or used as a public template source.

The VS Code workspace keeps this directory and the complete runtime tree visible.
Run `./cv structure` to verify the repository layout and privacy contract.

## Canonical files

- `master_cv.yaml`: lifelong career memory. Only eligible entries in
  `claim_registry` may supply factual résumé prose.
- `applications.yaml`: application stages and outcomes.
- `baseline_catalog.yaml`: optional role-family metadata for reusable layout baselines.
- `golden_packs.yaml`: user-defined Pack versions, approval state, source fingerprints,
  and exact CV/Portfolio/Combined PDF hashes. It is governance metadata, not evidence.

## Subdirectories

- `applications/<id>/`: one exact JD and its CV + cover-letter decision/claim/artifact manifest.
- `evidence/`: durable private proof such as degree records, contracts,
  certificates, thesis source, and historical source material.
- `inventory/`: dated discovery snapshots from GitHub or technical environments.
  Inventory is not résumé evidence until reviewed.
- `audits/`: dated private analyses and reconciliation reports.
- `chat/`: private source conversations retained for traceable research, never facts.
- `reapplication_batches/`: deliberate multi-role/reapplication planning records.

Within `evidence/`, use stable subject folders such as `education/`, `employment/`,
`certifications/`, and `legacy-cv/`. A historical CV is discovery material only: it
may help locate a forgotten fact, but it never overrides `claim_registry` or creates
an eligible claim without independent evidence or fresh owner confirmation.

Current TeX source belongs in `../workspace/current/`. Generated contexts and PDFs
belong in `../workspace/build/`; disposable render output belongs in
`../workspace/tmp/`; reusable clone-only layout references belong in `../workspace/baselines/`;
reviewed/freeze Golden source belongs in `../workspace/golden-packs/`; editable
application snapshots belong in `../workspace/profiles/`; closed history
belongs in `../archive/`. Recruiter-facing delivery copies belong in
`../output/pdf/applications/<application-id>/`; older layouts under `output/pdf/` remain
legacy/read-only. Delivery files are never factual authority. Run `./cv status`
before beginning a new application. Portfolio binaries live in ignored
`../assets/portfolio/{raw-private,raw,curated,generated}/`; their private user index may
live at `evidence/portfolio/ASSET_INDEX.md`. The tracked asset README is policy only.

Use `identity_anchors` in `master_cv.yaml` for durable evidence-bound credentials,
domains, market bridges, local fit, or autonomy that should survive JD tailoring.
Each application selects only one to three and records their placement.
Use `workspace/current/sections/order.tex` to change section priority per private profile.

`application_defaults` controls what a natural “new CV” request means. The public
default is `[cv, cover_letter]`; remove `cover_letter` only when résumé-only output is
an intentional owner decision. The manifest also records a capability include/omit
review so useful evidence-bound bonus skills cannot disappear silently. Schema 3.6
also stores `project_link_policy`: when a selected thesis has a public repository and
the policy is `required_when_public`, the final CV must expose that link using the
shared canonical project-link helper.

Schema 1.4 application manifests bind a vacancy to one registered Golden Pack, its
version, and exact CV SHA-256. A manifest cannot reach strict
`validated`, `sent`, or `closed` while the selected Pack is still a freeze candidate.

Schema 3.7 may also define `application_defaults.reusable_positioning`. Each phrase
must cite eligible claim IDs, name allowed role families and placements, and carry a
per-application use limit. This preserves reviewed recruiter positioning across agents
without turning prose into a new fact or encouraging a public gap inventory.

Schema 3.9 defines `application_defaults.work_authorization_policy`. Its exact compact
text is mandatory in every CV as a separate top identity/contact line and is verified
from the final PDF. Keep longer permit, validity, or residence-transition answers in the
application form when asked.
